## Table Operations

### Available Operations
- `create_table`: Create new table `{name, databaseId, description}`
- `read_table`: Get table schema and metadata by `table_id`
- `update_table`: Update table `{name, description}`
- `delete_table`: Delete table (WARNING: deletes all rows and data!)
- `list_tables`: List all tables, optionally filter by `database_id`

### Example

```python
# Create a new table
table_crud(method="create_table", data={
    "name": "Contacts",
    "databaseId": 5,
    "description": "Customer contact information"
})

# Read table schema (to see fields/columns)
table_crud(method="read_table", table_id="42")

# List all tables in a database
table_crud(method="list_tables", filters={"databaseId": 5})

# Update table metadata
table_crud(method="update_table", table_id="42", data={
    "name": "Customer Contacts",
    "description": "Updated description"
})

# Delete a table (careful - this removes all data!)
table_crud(method="delete_table", table_id="42")
```

### Important Notes

- Use `read_table` to see the table schema including all field names and types
- Table IDs are numeric
- Deleting a table permanently removes all rows and field definitions
